 "notes": "Cuts: the most important Irish whistle ornament. A cut is a finger flicked off a hole above the note for an instant, which separates repeated notes without tonguing. The first half practises it in the low octave and the second half in the high octave. Go slowly; the flick should be quick, not loud.",
